=== new nonesuch --title "A kind nobody declared"

refused, KindUnknown
  no kind is named `nonesuch`. This taxonomy declares `addressed`, `ambiguous`, `annexed`, `chaptered`, `decision_record`, `deeper`, `design_spec`, `exhausted`, `holed`, `misplaced`, `note`, `numbered`, `orphan`, `standalone`, `standard`, `unmintable`, `unopened_record`

=== new governed_document --title "An abstract kind"

refused, KindAbstract
  `governed_document` is abstract, and an abstract kind is a kind that no document ever is

=== new orphan --title "A kind on no shelf"

refused, KindUnshelved
  no shelf claims `orphan`, so a document of it would land where the census reads it back as something else. Declare a shelf for the kind first

=== new ambiguous --title "A kind on two shelves"

refused, KindOnManyShelves
  `ambiguous` sits on `first_claim`, `second_claim`, and nothing states which one a new document joins

=== new misplaced --title "A shelf that globs early"

refused, ShelfPathNotLiteral
  the shelf `misplacements` declares `corpus/*/misplaced/**`, and a glob before the last segment names no directory to write into

=== new holed --title "A layout with nothing to fill it"

refused, LayoutUnresolved
  the shelf `holes` declares `{seq:04d}-{slug}.md`, and `{seq:04d}` names neither a facet this document carries nor the sequence of the identifier it mints. A file name with a hole in it is not a name this verb writes

=== new decision_record --title ""

refused, TitleEmpty
  the title is empty, and the file name and the document's name both come from it

=== new unopened_record --title "A regime with no initial state"

refused, FacetUndeterminable
  `unopened_record` requires the facet `status`, and no lifecycle regime that this kind binds declares an `initial` state. A prompt in that field is a value the checks refuse, so this run writes nothing

=== new chaptered --title "An integer nothing derives"

refused, FacetUndeterminable
  `chaptered` requires the facet `chapter`, and it is declared `type: integer`, and a prompt is not one. A prompt in that field is a value the checks refuse, so this run writes nothing

=== new addressed --title "A closed set nothing derives"

refused, FacetUndeterminable
  `addressed` requires the facet `audience`, and it declares a closed value set and it carries no role this engine derives a value for. A prompt in that field is a value the checks refuse, so this run writes nothing

=== new unmintable --title "A pattern that cannot be read"

refused, SchemeUnreadable
  the scheme `broken_id` cannot be read: the pattern `BAD-{slug}-{namespace}` writes `{slug}` before another segment, and a free token has no stated end

=== new exhausted --title "A sequence field that is full"

refused, MintRefused
  the identifier this run built is one the scheme `exhausted_id` does not admit: the next sequence value is 100, and `EX-FIX-00` holds 2 digits. That is a defect in the scaffolder rather than in the declaration

=== new annexed --title "A layout that lands on another shelf"

refused, PlacementDoesNotResolve
  corpus/annexes/deep/a-layout-that-lands-on-another-shelf.md classifies as a document of the shelf `deeps` rather than as `annexed`, so the placement this run derived is not the placement the census reads. That is a defect in the scaffolder

=== new standard --title "A relation endpoint with no scheme"

refused, Unnameable
  `standard` names no identifier scheme, and `supersedes`, `assesses`, `traces_to` may name a document of it. Such a document is neither end of any edge, which `identifier.unusable` reports on every run. Declare `kinds.standard.identifier` first

=== new design_spec --title "The first part"

refused, IdentifierTaken
  `SPEC-FIX-the-first-part` is already declared on corpus/spec/01-the-first-part.md, and an identifier is never reused

=== new decision_record --title "An earlier decision"

refused, PathTaken
  corpus/decisions/an-earlier-decision.md is already there, and this verb never overwrites a document

=== new decision_record --title "A relation nobody declared" --relates flibberty=DR-FIX-0007

refused, RelationUnknown
  no relation is named `flibberty`. This taxonomy declares `assesses`, `refines`, `supersedes`

=== new decision_record --title "An edge a hook pays for" --relates traces_to=DR-FIX-0007

refused, RelationNotScaffolded
  `traces_to` declares `created_by: hook`, and this verb proposes the edges the taxonomy assigns to a scaffold. Write it by hand, or change what the declaration says pays for it

=== new decision_record --title "A source end the relation forbids" --relates refines=SPEC-FIX-the-first-part

refused, EndpointNotPermitted
  `refines` does not admit `decision_record` at its source end, which admits `design_spec`

=== new design_spec --title "A target end the relation forbids" --relates refines=DR-FIX-0007

refused, EndpointNotPermitted
  `refines` does not admit `decision_record` at its target end, which admits `design_spec`

=== new decision_record --title "A target that resolves to nothing" --relates supersedes=DR-FIX-9999

refused, TargetUnresolved
  `supersedes` names `DR-FIX-9999`, and no document of this corpus carries that identifier

